UFIS-NA meta-user layer
=======================

This layer contains UFIS-specific customizations for the `ufis_na_linux`
PetaLinux project.

Main contents
=============

Applications (`recipes-apps`)
-----------------------------

- `ufis-bitstream-manager`
  - Installs and enables `ufis-bitstream-manager.service`
  - Runs `/usr/bin/ufis_bitstream_server.py` on boot (TCP port `5001`)
  - Supports remote bitstream load through `fpgautil -b`

- `ufis-hw-tools`
  - Installs low-level diagnostics and monitoring tools:
    - `ufis-hw-scan`
    - `ufis-reg`
    - `ufis-health`
    - `ufis-mem-bench`
    - `ufis-irq-stat`
    - `ufis-logic-monitor`

- `nisl-achermann-branding`
  - Installs `/usr/bin/ufis_status`
  - Installs `/usr/bin/ufis_net_init`
  - Installs and enables `ufis-net-init.service` (DHCP with static fallback)

Core file overrides (`recipes-core`)
------------------------------------

- `base-files` bbappend
  - Installs custom `/etc/motd` banner (UFIS-NA branding)

Board support (`recipes-bsp`)
-----------------------------

- Device tree append files and `system-user.dtsi`
- U-Boot append with `platform-top.h` and `bsp.cfg`

Kernel (`recipes-kernel`)
-------------------------

- Linux append file with optional `bsp.cfg`

Rootfs integration
==================

UFIS packages are selected through:

- `conf/user-rootfsconfig`

Details and user-facing documentation are available at project root:

- `../../README.md`
- `../../docs/UFIS_TOOLS_REFERENCE.md`
- `../../docs/UFIS_ARCHITECTURE.md`
